        <div class="faq-accordion">
          <div class="faq-item active">
            <h3 class="faq-question">What luxury amenities are included in the Erg Chebbi desert camp?</h3>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Our handpicked luxury desert camps feature spacious private canvas pavilions with plush King or Queen beds, handcrafted Moroccan carpets, private en-suite bathrooms with hot-water showers, flushing porcelain toilets, electricity, bedside USB charging, and heating or AC. You also enjoy a candlelit 4-course Moroccan dinner and live campfire Gnawa drum performances under the stars.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3 class="faq-question">How long is the camel trek to reach the luxury camp?</h3>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>The sunset camel trek into the Erg Chebbi dunes takes approximately 45 to 60 minutes, timed perfectly for golden hour photography across the sand sea. For travelers who prefer not to ride camels or have mobility concerns, a private 4x4 dune transfer directly to your luxury tent entrance is always included at no extra charge.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3 class="faq-question">What is the driving time between Marrakech and the Sahara Desert?</h3>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>The journey covers approximately 560 km each way through the High Atlas, Dades Valley, and Todra Gorge. To ensure comfortable travel without rushing, our 3-Day Sahara Luxury Explorer breaks the drive with an overnight stay at a boutique kasbah hotel in Dades on Night 1, arriving at the Erg Chebbi dunes in the afternoon on Day 2.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3 class="faq-question">Can this Sahara tour end in Fes instead of returning to Marrakech?</h3>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Yes! Many travelers book our 3-Day or 4-Day Desert route starting in Marrakech and finishing in Fes (or vice versa). On the final day, your private driver chauffeurs you north across the Ziz Valley gorge, the Middle Atlas cedar forest of Azrou, and the Alpine town of Ifrane, arriving in Fes by early evening.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <h3 class="faq-question">Can dietary requirements (vegetarian, vegan, gluten-free, halal) be accommodated?</h3>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <p>Yes, all meals (both at kasbah stops and at the desert camp) are freshly prepared and can easily accommodate vegetarian, vegan, gluten-free, dairy-free, and nut-allergy requirements. Simply inform us when booking and your private hosts will curate tailored menus.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
